<dialog class="help-dialog" id="helpDialog"><div class="dialog-header"><div><div class="eyebrow">GETTING STARTED</div><h2>Dashboard kaise use karein</h2></div><button aria-label="Close help" class="close-button" data-close="helpDialog">×</button></div><div class="help-content"><h3>Ageing report: day-wise aur customer-wise</h3><p>Ageing analysis tab mein 0-30, 31-60, 61-90, 91-180, 181-365 aur 365+ days ke amounts aur open bill rows hain. 0 means aaj due hai; 365+ means 366 din ya zyada. Future due dates Not yet due mein alag hain. Missing dates bhi alag dikhte hain. Calculation due date se hoti hai, invoice date se nahi.</p><p>Bucket card par click karke filter lagayein; dobara click karke hata dein. Cards doosre filters ke saath poori distribution dikhate hain; neeche ki summary aur customer table selected bucket follow karte hain. Customer table mein amount par click karke us bracket ke bills dekhein. Export summary bucket report deta hai; upar Export CSV customer-wise ageing deta hai.</p>
<h3>1. Seedha browser mein kholein</h3><p>Portal ko browser link se kholein. Login required hai; access admin permissions ke hisaab se milta hai.</p>
<h3>2. Search aur filters lagayein</h3><p>Customer name, bill number ya remarks search karein. Coordinator aur customer type select karein. Top bar ke <strong>Date filter</strong> dropdown mein <strong>Due Date</strong>, <strong>Invoice Date</strong> ya <strong>Invoice OR Due Date</strong> choose karein, phir wahi <strong>From / To</strong> range use karein. More filters mein Quick date range se Current week, Previous week ya Current month bhi select kar sakte hain. Current week Monday-Sunday ke hisaab se automatically banta hai. Reset se saare filters hat jayenge.</p>
<h3>3. Week-wise Collection Summary</h3><p><strong>Week-wise Summary</strong> tab har month ko 4 management weeks (1-7, 8-14, 15-21, 22-month end) me divide karta hai. Total Outstanding aur TTL O/Due week start position se automatically reconstruct hote hain; Received Receipt Date se, Collection % = Received / TTL O/Due, BM default 80%, aur Total = Received + Credit Note + RTV + Write Off + Other. Week par click karke us range ke bill-wise records khol sakte hain.</p>
<h3>4. Customer aur bill details dekhein</h3><p>Top 5 mein customer par click karke uske bills kholein. Bill register mein bill number par click karein: payment, due date, remarks aur follow-up details dikhenge.</p>
<h3>Over due aur Party wise remark</h3><p>Over due tab sirf positive overdue bills dikhata hai. Party wise remark tab mein har party ke saamne follow-up remark type kar sakte hain. Ab auto-save band hai: Edit par click karein, remark likhein, phir Save par click karein. Clear Remark se sirf remark clear hota hai; History se purane changes dikhte hain; Save dashboard copy se saved remarks HTML file mein embed ho jaate hain.</p>
<h3>PR register, PO tracker, POD tracker aur GRN tracker</h3><p>PR Register aur PO Tracker uploaded PO-FMS Sheet55 se chal rahe hain. Ye data receivables live Google Sheet se alag rakha gaya hai, isliye Sync Google Sheet ya Receivables Dashboard par koi effect nahi padega. GRN Tracker ab PR/PO Sheet55 ke GRN columns se live/JSON source par chal raha hai. POD tracker future dedicated source se connect kiya ja sakta hai.</p>
<h3>4. Amount aur date badlein</h3><p>INR selector se Lakh, Rupees ya Crore choose karein. Ageing date badalne par due/overdue classification badlegi; stored payment aur pending balances nahi badlenge. Purani date par balance historical outstanding nahi hai.</p>
<h3>5. Fresh Excel se update karein</h3><p>Import / Merge Excel par click karke isi layout ki nayi .xlsx file select karein. Purana unique data preserve rahega; same Party + Ref. No. wale records duplicate nahi banenge aur latest upload wali values se refresh honge. File mein Data sheet aur Party ya Customer Name + Pending Amount headers rehne chahiye. Optional TDS column ke liye header TDS, TDS Amount ya TDS Deduction use karein. Admin import browser mein parse hota hai aur secure login ke through server par save hota hai. Purane .xls, encrypted ya password-protected workbooks supported nahi hain.</p>
<h3>Master Data</h3><p>Excel import/merge ke baad sidebar ka <strong>Master Data</strong> menu current saved source ke saare rows aur columns dikhata hai. Re-upload par merged/deduplicated result yahi master me nazar aayega.</p><h3>6. Update ko save aur share karein</h3><p>Import ke baad neeche Save dashboard copy click karein. Nayi HTML file mein updated data embed ho jayega. Browser band karne par bina save kiye updates kho jayenge. Export CSV selected view ke saare filtered records export karta hai, sirf current page nahi.</p>
<div class="notice warning">Ye live Excel / Google Sheets connection nahi hai. Fresh balances ke liye Admin Import / Merge Excel use kare. User access server login aur permissions se controlled hai.</div>
<h3>Calculation basis</h3><p>Net O/S = OLD Pending Amount minus Debit Note minus Receipt Amount (Data!G - I - J), where those inputs are available. The saved Pending Amount is used when inputs are unavailable. Overdue means Due Date &lt; Ageing as of. Due today is not overdue, but enters the 0-30 ageing bucket. Future due dates enter Not yet due. Exactly 365 days is in 181-365; 365+ starts at day 366. Negative balances remain in net totals; open bill rows count positive balances. Receipts are recorded ledger amounts, not a monthly collection measure.</p>
</div></dialog>
<div aria-live="polite" class="toast" hidden="" id="toast" role="status"></div>
